---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import EventStream from '../../components/EventStream.astro';
import PageNext from '../../components/PageNext.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../../components/CtaBlock.astro';
---

<Layout title="Session discipline — never start building unrecorded" pathname="/features/discipline">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow-chain">
        <span class="eyebrow">Feature</span>
        <span class="eyebrow-sep">·</span>
        <span class="eyebrow-dim">maddu hooks install</span>
        <span class="eyebrow-sep">·</span>
        <span class="eyebrow-dim">since v1.89.0</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Every session on the record. <span class="dim-h1">Before the first edit.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Hooks register a session the moment it starts, checkpoint governance before every context compaction, and — since v1.97.0 — <strong>block a mutating edit</strong> when a session ritual is stale. Discipline you have to remember isn't discipline; Máddu enforces it.
      </p>
      <pre class="feat-cli"><code>$ maddu hooks install
wired SessionStart · SessionEnd · PreCompact · PreToolUse into .claude/settings.json</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">§ 01 · The problem</span>
        <h2>Discipline you have to remember isn't discipline.</h2>
        <p>
          A session that forgets to register leaves no record of what it touched. Worse, a context compaction can drop the last un-recorded work silently — and you only notice when the trail is already gone.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="panel-title">Start records itself</span>
            <span class="panel-aside">automatic</span>
          </div>
          <p><code>SessionStart</code> auto-registers a session and writes it to the spine; <code>SessionEnd</code> closes it. No manual <code>--session</code> flag to forget — the record exists before you type the first prompt.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="panel-title">Compaction leaves a mark</span>
            <span class="panel-aside">since v1.89.0</span>
          </div>
          <p><code>PreCompact</code> writes a <code>COMPACTION_CHECKPOINT</code> before every compaction — manual <code>/compact</code> and automatic alike — capturing the last <code>slice-stop</code> as the durable anchor: anything after it that wasn't recorded did not survive.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="panel-title">It never breaks you</span>
            <span class="panel-aside">fails open</span>
          </div>
          <p>The hooks never exit <code>2</code>. A governance instrument must never crash the session it observes — any evaluator, git, or parse error degrades to allow. Enforcement can only <em>deny an edit through a structured decision</em>, never break the tool.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <Callout tone="accent-2" title="The checkpoint knows what's at risk" tag="compaction-checkpoint">
        <p>
          Each checkpoint records the trigger, the last recorded <code>slice-stop</code>, handoff currency, open approvals, and active claims. <code>maddu orient</code> auto-announces the latest one on session start, and doctor validates that the hook stanza is still current.
        </p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">§ 02 · The enforcement gate · since v1.97.0</span>
        <h2>Governance stopped being advisory.</h2>
        <p>
          The <code>PreToolUse</code> hook evaluates the session's rituals before every <strong>mutating</strong> tool call — the edit tools always, and <code>Bash</code> only when the command is a recognized write (<code>&gt;</code>/<code>&gt;&gt;</code> redirects, <code>sed -i</code>, <code>tee</code>, <code>mv</code>/<code>cp</code>/<code>rm</code>, PowerShell <code>Set-Content</code>…). If a ritual is stale, it <strong>denies the edit</strong> and names the exact remedy. Reads and the remedy commands themselves are never gated, so a block can't deadlock its own fix.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="panel-title">Ordered blockers</span>
            <span class="panel-aside">first-stale wins</span>
          </div>
          <p>session → lane → governing goal/plan → slice-stop freshness → uncommitted pileup. The deny names the <em>first</em> stale ritual only, with its exact remedy — <code>maddu register</code>, <code>lane claim</code>, <code>goal set</code>, <code>plan</code>, or <code>slice-stop</code>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="panel-title">Tier-scaled</span>
            <span class="panel-aside">governance mode</span>
          </div>
          <p><code>strict</code> blocks at the first threshold; <code>standard</code> is <em>graduated</em> — block a missing session/lane now, warn then block on a stale slice-stop or commit pileup; <code>relaxed</code> only nudges. One governance value, <code>discipline-enforcement</code>, sets it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="panel-title">Gates before done</span>
            <span class="panel-aside">strict</span>
          </div>
          <p>At enforcing tiers, <code>maddu goal done</code> and <code>maddu plan complete</code> run the gate suite first and refuse to close while a required gate is red. <code>abandon</code>/<code>cancel</code> are honest terminal states and are never gated.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <Callout tone="accent" title="Block-and-tell — never auto-perform" tag="pre-tool-use">
        <p>
          Máddu never auto-slice-stops or auto-commits to satisfy a gate — that would fake the record. Enforcement is <strong>block-and-tell</strong>: it stops the edit and hands you the one command that clears the block. The companion <code>discipline-observed</code> doctor gate flags a repo that pins a tier but never wired the hook — where enforcement silently does nothing. Back out any time with <code>maddu hooks uninstall</code>.
        </p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">§ 03 · On the record</span>
        <h2>What a disciplined session looks like on the spine.</h2>
      </header>
      <EventStream
        eyebrow="Session start to close, checkpoint in between"
        source=".maddu/events/2026-07-05.ndjson"
        entries={[
          { time: '08:31:04.212', type: 'SESSION_REGISTERED',      tone: 'session',  payload: 'role=implementer · trigger=SessionStart',              actor: 'claude-code' },
          { time: '09:02:47.883', type: 'SLICE_STOPPED',           tone: 'approval', payload: 'targets=discipline.astro · gates=7 pass',              actor: 'claude-code' },
          { time: '09:18:22.109', type: 'COMPACTION_CHECKPOINT',   tone: 'accent',   payload: 'trigger=auto · anchor=SLICE_STOPPED@09:02 · approvals=0', actor: 'claude-code' },
          { time: '09:44:51.640', type: 'SESSION_CLOSED',          tone: 'session',  payload: 'trigger=SessionEnd · duration=73m',                    actor: 'claude-code' },
        ]}
      />
      <p class="feat-note">
        Related verbs: <a href="/capabilities/hooks"><code>maddu hooks</code></a> · <a href="/capabilities/agents"><code>maddu agents</code></a> · <a href="/capabilities/orient"><code>maddu orient</code></a> · <a href="/capabilities/session"><code>maddu session</code></a>
      </p>
      <p class="feat-note">
        Companion verb: <a href="/capabilities/agents"><code>maddu agents</code></a> registers a self-contained "install maddu" stanza into your global agent instruction files — Claude, Codex, Gemini, or a custom path — so the framework is reachable by natural language from any future repo.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-narrow">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="btn" href="/docs/features/discipline">Read the full reference in the docs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <PageNext
    eyebrow="Next feature"
    title="Earned autonomy — trust is earned on the record, not asserted."
    hint="A deterministic per-lane trust score over the verified record, recommend-only by contract."
    href="/features/autonomy"
    tone="accent"
  />
  <CtaBlock />
</Layout>

<style>
  .feat-cli {
    margin: var(--m-space-5) 0 0;
    padding: var(--m-space-4) var(--m-space-5);
    background: var(--m-bg-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--m-line);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--m-accent);
    border-radius: var(--m-radius);
    font-family: var(--m-font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--m-fg-1);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .feat-note {
    margin-top: var(--m-space-5);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--m-fg-2);
  }
  .feat-note code { font-size: 12px; }
</style>
